Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 09:15:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Move AutofillElements out of the Cocoa folder Need the bug
 URL (OOPS!).

Reviewed by NOBODY (OOPS!).

GLib ports need a way to autofill login forms that does not rely on a
web process extension and fits site isolation. This change prepares for
that by moving AutofillElements, which Cocoa uses to find the user name
and password fields of a login form and fill them, out of the Cocoa
folder, so that every port builds it. Nothing in it is Cocoa specific.
A following change adds the GLib API on top of it.

* Source/WebCore/Headers.cmake:
* Source/WebCore/Sources.txt:
* Source/WebCore/SourcesCocoa.txt:
* Source/WebCore/WebCore.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj:
* Source/WebCore/editing/AutofillElements.cpp: Renamed from Source/WebCore/editing/cocoa/AutofillElements.cpp.
* Source/WebCore/editing/AutofillElements.h: Renamed from Source/WebCore/editing/cocoa/AutofillElements.h.
